  "protocol": {
    "tasks": "Three native AppKit workflows, two datasets each, paired cu and actual Codex native App API. One fresh Codex task per attempt; initialization then one measured GO turn.",
    "isolation": "Fresh app executable path, unique bundle identifier, PID, saved file, and task. cu additionally has a fresh Broker directory, task client key and output directory. Same OS/permissions/system caches, no VM or reboot.",
    "timing": "Recorded Codex task durations. setup_ms covers initialization; execution_ms covers full GO turn; combined_turn_ms sums those turns, excluding coordinator gaps, fixture build/start and independent verification.",
    "execution": "Sequential participants, alternating intended first arm. Two isolation deviations retained separately and replaced after their paired native trial. No timing/correctness feedback or solver supplied.",
    "model": "All setup/GO turns: gpt-6-astra, high reasoning, no service-tier override.",
    "scope": "Controlled custom native interfaces supporting AX value writes. Not real browser, Electron or commercial-app performance.",
    "metrics": "Model calls count unique response usage records. Tool calls/errors/intervals cover recorded CommandExecution and McpToolCall events; caught/logical errors and file-patch events may not count. Output characters count text only. Input tokens include cached repeated context; not a cost estimate. Non-tool intervals include model, network and scheduling; not pure inference.",
    "limitations": "Two samples per arm/task; no confidence interval or universal speed claim. Different seed inputs and uncontrolled backend latency/strategy affect timing. Replacement order is not fully counterbalanced."
